@startuml
title MES order list caching with Cache-Aside

actor Operator
boundary "MES Dashboard" as Dashboard
control "MES API" as API
database "Redis\nList cache" as Redis
database "MES DB\nSource of truth" as DB

== Read the order list ==

Operator -> Dashboard: Open or refresh the order list
Dashboard -> API: GET /orders?filters&sort&page
API -> DB: Read orders_list cache version
DB --> API: version = 42
API -> API: Derive access scope from authorization context\nand build key from version, filters, sort and page
API -> Redis: GET mes:orders:list:v42:{query-hash}

alt Cache hit
    Redis --> API: Cached order list
    API --> Dashboard: 200 OK, order list
else Cache miss
    Redis --> API: Key not found
    API -> DB: SELECT current order list
    DB --> API: Current order list
    API -> Redis: SET key, serialized list, EX 5 minutes
    Redis --> API: OK
    API --> Dashboard: 200 OK, order list
else Redis unavailable
    Redis --> API: Connection error
    API -> DB: SELECT current order list
    DB --> API: Current order list
    API --> Dashboard: 200 OK, order list
    API -> API: Record cache error metric and log
end

Dashboard --> Operator: Display the order list

== Change the order status ==

Operator -> Dashboard: Change order status
Dashboard -> API: PATCH /orders/{id}/status
note over API, DB
  Dashboard, B2B and RabbitMQ commands use the same write path.
end note
API -> DB: BEGIN
API -> DB: UPDATE order status
API -> DB: INCREMENT orders_list cache version

alt Transaction committed
    API -> DB: COMMIT
    DB --> API: Status saved, version = 43
    note over Redis
      Keys with v42 are no longer reachable.
      They will be removed by TTL.
    end note
    API --> Dashboard: 200 OK, updated order
    Dashboard --> Operator: Display the new status
else Database error
    API -> DB: ROLLBACK
    DB --> API: Status and version unchanged
    API --> Dashboard: Error response
    Dashboard --> Operator: Show update error
end

@enduml
